==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wargod Mitsuhide''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Immortal Mitsuhide''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
While Akechi Mitsuhide can be used as a generalist, his true value comes from his ability to knock Dark and Angel enemies back without fail. His Long Distance allows him to snipe even backliners such as [[Sunfish Jones]] and [[Le'noir]] instead of pushing into their range. His Long Distance has a rather large blind spot, however, so fierce melee enemies such as [[Angelic Gory]] or [[Gory Dark]], for example, will only continue to push, therefore properly defending Mitsuhide with strong melee-to-midrange fighters is a must. In his Evolved Form, he can also unleash a surge that has a chance to hit inside the blind spot, though this is not guaranteed and only has a 50% chance of activation in any case. It can definitely be a nice bonus, but it is far from reliable.

As with all [[:Category:Cats with Conjure ability|Conjurers]], Mitsuhide cannot be stacked. In exchange is a one-time spirit that can cover his blind spot when things get dicey.

==='''True Form'''===
Consistency is the name of the game, and Immortal Mitsuhide delivers with a 100% chance to create a [[Surge Attack]], boosting his DPS by 25% up to ~6,850. Along with that is [[Immune to Wave|Wave Immunity]], facilitating matchups against [[Two Can]], [[Youcan]], while also improving generalist usage against [[Kory]] variants. The HP and [[Conjure]] buffs are fairly small, but make him that much more reliable. All in all, a good True Form for a very low price.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Sniper}}

